# JOVRA isolated-test tester allow-list, format v1.
#
# This file is an example of the format. The real list is `testers.allowlist` in this folder; it is gitignored and
# never committed, because it holds real testers' addresses. The operator (Jon) keeps it, and at gate G1 the
# operator script reads it to create each tester through the admin API and to fill app_ops.tester_allowlist with
# the HMAC of each address. The addresses themselves are never stored in the database or logged.
#
# Rules:
# - One email address per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# - Each address is trimmed and lower-cased before hashing, so case and surrounding spaces do not matter.
# - No passwords, names or other fields: testers sign in with an email one-time code (ADR-0022).
# - A tester removed from the list can no longer be created, but an existing account must also be deleted.
#
# The local stack does not read this file; seed/00_testers.sql creates the same fictional testers directly.
owner.tester@example.test
coach.tester@example.test
viewer.tester@example.test
camera.tester@example.test
unrelated.tester@example.test
pending.tester@example.test
